  "body": "Minor cleanup:\n\nIn the section on [HTML parsing](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#parsing) there is a long note that ends with \"Authors interested in using SGML tools in their authoring pipeline are encouraged to use XML tools and the XML serialization of HTML.\" It seems odd to encourage the use of an unmaintained syntax which is not recommended for use. Perhaps change this to read \"Use of SGML tools for processing HTML is not recommended, but can be accomplished using the [XML syntax](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/xhtml.html#the-xhtml-syntax) when necessary.\"",
